  "evidence": "97 of 104 checks agree with a value taken on a console, byte for byte.",
  "howToSettleIt": "Four of the seven disagreements are the hidden envelope on the gain and key-on paths, and the same subsystem agrees on the ADSR path, which is where to look. Two more are one cause: V8 outx and V9 envx report the same pair of values. The seventh, Misc/$F0-$FF are not ram, is about the audio unit's register file rather than this part.",
  "producedBy": "A cut-down console driving the cartridge into a composed audio unit. It is not carried by any member of this family and deliberately so: a console processor does not belong in a model of the sound generator. sony-s-smp-python records why under what is deliberately not modelled. What is carried is this record, so the verdicts can be disputed without rebuilding the harness.",
  "howToRepeat": "Compose mos65xx-python with sony-s-smp-python, decode the cartridge as LoROM, wire $2140-$2143 to the unit's four ports, and watch for the four-byte comparison against $dc through $df that every one of his checks ends with."
